[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="QuestResource" load_steps=3 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Quests/QuestResource.cs" id="1_quest"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Quests/ObjectiveResource.cs" id="2_obj"]

; Ash Hunters field induction (Phase 42E). "The kill is the smallest part of it" — Yrsa Kesk's own
; line from her 42B greeting — is the whole design brief: two placed clues come before the den, and
; what the player does at the den is a judgment the investigation earns rather than a kill counter.
;
; ⚠️ NOT SequentialObjectives, ON PURPOSE, AND IT WAS THE FIRST DRAFT'S BUG. A Kill objective fires
; off a one-time EntityDiedEvent that never replays — so an obj_kill made "current" only after the
; clues and the debrief (the tidy story order) misses the death outright the moment a player finds
; the den before finishing either, and QuestLogComponent.Advance's IsObjectiveActive check then
; refuses it forever: no later objective in a Sequential quest can go active while an earlier LIVE one
; sits permanently short, which is a soft-lock with a green --validate. Every objective here is
; therefore independently gated by RequiredFlagId/ForbiddenFlagId alone, exactly the
; quest.hollowreach.barrels shape minus the ordering bool — a kill counts whenever it happens.
;
; ⚠️ obj_kill CARRIES NO RequiredFlagId. Halda's judgment sets the flag that would gate it, but a
; player is never blocked from defending themselves or striking first at the den before ever hearing
; the choice framed — this is a wild boar, not a puzzle lock. What obj_kill DOES carry is
; ForbiddenFlagId on the spare mark: once you have told Halda you will let it live, going back on
; that word no longer earns the guild's credit for it, which is the honesty the phase brief asks for.
;
; ⚠️ obj_report_kill GATES ON THE DEATH, NOT THE VERDICT. flag.ash_hunters.grimtusk_defeated is set by
; LairSpawnComponent.DefeatFlagId the instant the boar dies, spare mark or no judgment at all — so a
; player who stumbles on the den and kills it before ever meeting Halda can still walk the hide to
; Fell Ardan. This is also what makes "killed early" a real, completable state: the offering dialogue
; (dlg.hunter_tracker's boar_offer node) checks the same flag before it will even start this quest,
; and pays the induction outright rather than sending the player after a corpse — the
; quest.ancient.kin shape, one guild down.
;
; ⚠️ AllowsOneShotTarget: TRUE. The den is a lair (LairSpawnComponent, not encounter.boar_territory —
; a DIFFERENT template id, enemy.grimtusk, so the region's roaming thornback boars can never
; substitute for this one and a dead Grimtusk can never come back to be re-hunted.

